From adaea036442edb4ebab4241eef390a4221b72123 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Hartkopp <socketcan@hartkopp.net>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 20:33:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 32/35] can: isotp: check the data length of the last CF

A CF shorter than LL_DL is only allowed as last CF and therefore has to
carry all missing bytes of the PDU. But the missing bytes were compared
with the payload of a full CF. So a short CF without all missing bytes
was accepted and the reception continued with further CFs.

Drop a short CF when the missing PDU bytes exceed its possible payload
(datalen - ae - N_PCI_SZ). Padding is still possible as it only
increases datalen. isotp_rcv() ensures datalen >= ae + N_PCI_SZ, so
the payload size can not underflow.

Fixes: e057dd3fc20f ("can: add ISO 15765-2:2016 transport protocol")
Signed-off-by: Oliver Hartkopp <socketcan@hartkopp.net>
---
 net/can/isotp/protocolrx.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/net/can/isotp/protocolrx.c b/net/can/isotp/protocolrx.c
index 794f2b9..ae5db66 100644
--- a/net/can/isotp/protocolrx.c
+++ b/net/can/isotp/protocolrx.c
@@ -361,8 +361,10 @@ static void isotp_rcv_cf(struct sock *sk, u8 *data, unsigned int datalen,
 
 	/* CFs have usually the LL_DL length */
 	if (datalen < so->rx.ll_dl) {
-		/* this is only allowed for the last CF */
-		if (so->rx.len - so->rx.idx > so->rx.ll_dl - ae - N_PCI_SZ)
+		/* only the last CF may be shorter: drop it when the
+		 * missing PDU bytes exceed its possible payload
+		 */
+		if (so->rx.len - so->rx.idx > datalen - ae - N_PCI_SZ)
 			return;
 	}
 
